\pard\f1\fs32 Nico's Links - App Summary\par
\pard\fs6\par

\pard\f1\fs24 What it is\f0\fs22\par
\pard Nico's Links is a personal portfolio and utility web app for Nico Ruge, built as a client-side single-page site with route-based sections. It combines creative showcase pages with practical tools such as transit departures, travel mapping, and an X thread formatter.\par
\fs6\par

\pard\f1\fs24 Who it's for\f0\fs22\par
\pard Primary persona: Nico Ruge and visitors interested in his photography, travel activity, and personal web utilities.\par
\fs6\par

\pard\f1\fs24 What it does\f0\fs22\par
\pard\li300
\bullet\tab Presents a themed multi-section SPA shell (Home, Work, Projects, Other) with hash navigation and responsive sidebar.\par
\bullet\tab Shows a photography portfolio with Unsplash-backed carousels and lightbox links.\par
\bullet\tab Renders an interactive Mapbox travel map using local GeoJSON layers (trains, buses, ferry, sights) and filters.\par
\bullet\tab Provides live station lookup and departure boards via transport.rest API calls with mode filtering and refresh.\par
\bullet\tab Embeds Tumblr blog content with paging, detail view, and media lightbox.\par
\bullet\tab Includes an X Thread Viewer that builds a Reddit-style nested thread view from pasted X links.\par
\pard\li0
\fs6\par

\pard\f1\fs24 How it works (repo evidence)\f0\fs22\par
\pard\li300
\bullet\tab Frontend: static HTML + Vue 3 app in \f1 index.html\f0  that mounts page components from \f1 assets/js/page_*.js\f0 .\par
\bullet\tab UI/styling: Bootstrap 5 + custom CSS in \f1 css/index.css\f0  and \f1 css/pages.css\f0 ; assets in \f1 assets/icons\f0 , \f1 assets/fonts\f0 , \f1 assets/images\f0 .\par
\bullet\tab Data flow: browser fetches external APIs (transport.rest, Tumblr, X oEmbed, Tr\'e4welling) and local GeoJSON; widgets poll/update in client JS.\par
\bullet\tab Server-side helpers: Netlify Functions in \f1 netlify/functions\f0  expose Spotify status (credentialed) and Mapbox token endpoints used by frontend.\par
\bullet\tab Persistence/state: hash route + in-memory component state; theme preference stored in \f1 localStorage\f0 .\par
\pard\li0
\fs6\par

\pard\f1\fs24 How to run (minimal)\f0\fs22\par
\pard\li300
\bullet\tab Serve the repo root as a static site (for example: \f1 cd /Users/nicoruge/Documents/GitHub/NicosLinks3 && python3 -m http.server 8000\f0 ).\par
\bullet\tab Open \f1 http://localhost:8000\f0  and navigate sections via hash routes.\par
\bullet\tab Optional for full behavior: deploy with Netlify Functions and set env vars for Spotify/Mapbox tokens.\par
\bullet\tab Build scripts / package manager config: \f1 Not found in repo.\f0\par
\bullet\tab Automated test setup: \f1 Not found in repo.\f0\par
\pard\li0
